{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' runs/2026-07-04-module-03-manifest-dry-run/checkpoints/negative-control-without-notes/.receipts-category-progress.md\"","aggregated_output":"# receipts/group_expenses_by_category + --by-category CLI flag: progress\n\n## Status: DONE\n\nBoth tests in `tests/test_by_category.py` pass:\n\n```\ncd <hekton>/factory-output/terminal-velocity/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6a3dfbd30873279a/fixtures/receipts && PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m unittest tests.test_by_category -v\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\ntest_cli_by_category_flag_prints_category_totals ... ok\ntest_group_expenses_by_category_totals_and_counts ... ok\n\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\n\nOK\n```\n\n## What was found on resume\n\nA prior session had already implemented `group_expenses_by_category` in\n`receipts/grouping.py` (verified via `git diff` against the tracked baseline —\nit groups rows by the `category` field, reuses `_parse_row` for validation,\ncollects malformed rows into `errors`, and returns a `GroupResult` with\n`months` keyed by category name). That part was correct and untouched by me.\n\nWhat was still missing: `receipts/cli.py` had no `--by-category` flag at all.\nRunning `python3 -m unittest tests.test_by_category -v` before making the CLI\nchange would have failed the `test_cli_by_category_flag_prints_category_totals`\ntest (import would succeed, but `main([..., \"--by-category\"])` would raise\n`argparse` \"unrecognized arguments\"). I verified this reasoning by reading\n`receipts/cli.py` directly rather than trusting any stale assumption.\n\nNo `.receipts-category-progress.md` existed on disk when this session started\nin this directory, so there was no earlier claim to cross-check — this file is\nbeing created fresh.\n\n## What was done this session\n\nEdited `receipts/cli.py` only:\n- Imported `group_expenses_by_category` alongside `group_expenses_by_month`.\n- Added `parser.add_argument(\"--by-category\", action=\"store_true\", ...)`.\n- Branched on `args.by_category`: if set, call `group_expenses_by_category(rows)`;\n  otherwise (default, unchanged), call `group_expenses_by_month(rows, tz=args.tz)`.\n- Renamed the loop variable from `month` to the more generic `key` since it's\n  now either a month string or a category string, printing\n  `f\"{key}: {summary.count} receipt(s), total ${summary.total:.2f}\"` — the\n  format string itself is unchanged, so default (no-flag) output is byte-for-byte\n  identical to before.\n\nDid not touch `receipts/grouping.py` (already correct from the prior session).\nDid not touch anything under `tests/`, `SPEC.md`, `data/`, or outside\n`receipts/` in this fixture directory.\n\n## Verification performed\n\n1. `PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m unittest tests.test_by_category -v` -> both tests pass.\n2. Manually ran `python3 -m receipts.cli data/sample_receipts.csv` (no flag) to\n   confirm default month-grouping behavior is unchanged/still works.\n3. Manually ran `python3 -m receipts.cli data/sample_receipts.csv --by-category`\n   to confirm category output looks sane (prints `meals:`, `travel:` lines).\n4. `git status` before and after: only `receipts/cli.py` and `receipts/grouping.py`\n   show as modified within this fixture's `receipts/` package. Other repo-wide\n   diffs/untracked files (e.g. `runs/.schema.yaml`, `modules/03-harness-engineering/...`)\n   were already present before this session touched anything and are unrelated\n   to this task — left alone.\n\n## Nothing left to do for this task's scope.\n\nIf someone resumes this: re-run the verification command above yourself before\ntrusting this file. If it still passes and `git status` still shows only\n`receipts/cli.py` + `receipts/grouping.py` changed inside `receipts/`, the task\nis complete.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
