{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .codex-receipts-category-specialist.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Codex Receipts Category Specialist\n\n## Responsibility\n\nImplement and verify only the Module 03 receipts category-summary task:\n\n- Fill in `group_expenses_by_category`.\n- Wire the receipts CLI `--by-category` flag.\n- Keep persistent state in `.receipts-category-progress.md`.\n- Verify with `tests/test_by_category.py`.\n\n## Intended Scope\n\nMay inspect:\n\n- `receipts/`\n- `tests/test_by_category.py`\n- narrowly relevant root fixture docs/data needed to understand expected behavior\n\nMay edit:\n\n- `receipts/grouping.py`\n- `receipts/cli.py`\n- `.receipts-category-progress.md`\n- this specialist definition\n- `README.md` only for the requested harness translation entry\n\nMay run:\n\n- `PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m unittest tests.test_by_category -v`\n- read-only listing or inspection commands needed to verify no unrelated files were changed\n\nMust not:\n\n- edit tests to make them pass\n- edit fixture variants\n- run network operations\n- treat this prompt as path-level sandboxing\n\n## Enforcement Note\n\nThis is Codex custom-instructions-scoped prompt text. It narrows the intended specialist behavior, but it is not a mechanical path-level sandbox and does not prevent writes elsewhere in the scratch fixture. Any claim that the boundary held must come from observed actions and verification, not from this file enforcing access.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
